 "text": "The U.S. government once paid psychics to spy for it, for over 20 years. It was called Project Stargate. Soldiers at Fort Meade tried to see enemy bases with their minds. Cost? About $20 million. In 1995, an independent review found it never once guided an intelligence operation. Here's the trick. Their reports were vague. And vague feels accurate, because your brain fills in the rest. That's how horoscopes work too. Follow for more dark psychology.",
